      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the labeled maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you do intend a dose above the labeled maximum, it will need to go through pharmacy or the prescriber's own review. I can't enter it on an unverified statement."
      }
